## DialogServiceExtensions

**Namespace**: `Cyrena.Extensions`
**Assembly**: `Cyrena.Components.Core`

### Purpose
Extension methods on `IDialogService` for showing MudBlazor dialogs with a simplified confirmation pattern. Returns a boolean indicating whether the user confirmed (not canceled) the dialog.

### Class Definition

```csharp
public static class DialogServiceExtensions
{
    public static async Task<bool> ShowDialogAsync<TComponent>(
        this IDialogService dialog, 
        string title, 
        DialogParameters parameters, 
        MaxWidth maxWidth = MaxWidth.Medium)
        where TComponent : ComponentBase;
}
```

### Methods

#### `ShowDialogAsync<TComponent>(string title, DialogParameters parameters, MaxWidth maxWidth = MaxWidth.Medium)`

```csharp
public static async Task<bool> ShowDialogAsync<TComponent>(
    this IDialogService dialog, 
    string title, 
    DialogParameters parameters, 
    MaxWidth maxWidth = MaxWidth.Medium)
    where TComponent : ComponentBase;
```

Shows a MudBlazor dialog and returns `true` if the user confirmed (not canceled), `false` otherwise.

**Parameters:**
- `dialog`: The `IDialogService` instance (typically injected)
- `title`: Dialog title displayed in the header
- `parameters`: `DialogParameters` instance containing component parameters
- `maxWidth`: Maximum dialog width (default: `MaxWidth.Medium`)

**Returns:** `Task<bool>` — `true` if user confirmed, `false` if canceled or null result

**Implementation Details:**
- Sets `FullWidth = true` automatically
- Awaits `dialog.Result`
- Returns `false` if result is null or `result.Canceled == true`
- Returns `true` for any non-canceled result

### Usage Example

```csharp
// In a Blazor component
[Inject] private IDialogService _dialog { get; set; } = default!;

public async Task ShowMyDialog()
{
    var parameters = new DialogParameters<MyDialogForm>
    {
        { x => x.Model, model }
    };

    var confirmed = await _dialog.ShowDialogAsync<MyDialogForm>("Dialog Title", parameters);

    if (confirmed)
    {
        // User clicked Submit — model has been modified
        await _store.UpdateAsync(model);
    }
}
```

### Important Notes
- This is a **simplified helper** for confirmation-style dialogs
- For dialogs that need to return complex data, use `IDialogService.ShowAsync<T>()` directly and inspect `DialogResult.Data`
- The dialog component (`TComponent`) must follow the MudBlazor dialog form pattern (see API Reference `mudblazor-dialog-form-pattern`)
- Uses `DialogParameters` (non-generic) in the signature, but callers typically pass `DialogParameters<TComponent>`

### Related
- `IDialogService` — MudBlazor dialog service
- `DialogParameters` / `DialogParameters<T>` — MudBlazor dialog parameter types
- `DialogResult` — MudBlazor dialog result type
- API Reference `mudblazor-dialog-form-pattern` — Authoritative dialog form pattern
